easing one half of a diagonal after STOP re-issues motion", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L262"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_04_release_all_jog_keys_clears_trace_frame_s_borrowed_jog_busy_go_scale_stops_then_resumes_moving_on_its_own", "label": "MOT-04 - release_all_jog_keys clears trace_frame's borrowed _jog_busy: Go Scale stops, then resumes moving on its own", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L333"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_05_d8_01_is_assumed_to_halt_an_interactive_d9_10_rapid_the_only_in_repo_decoder_says_it_is_a_process_stop_that_does_not_touch_motion", "label": "MOT-05 - D8 01 is assumed to halt an interactive D9 10 rapid; the only in-repo decoder says it is a process stop that does not touch motion", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L411"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_06_a_key_up_can_be_overtaken_by_the_key_down_it_is_releasing_d9_run_to_limit_lands_after_d8_01", "label": "MOT-06 - A key-up can be overtaken by the key-down it is releasing: D9 run-to-limit lands after D8 01", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L500"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_07_held_jog_and_step_jog_drive_the_head_to_the_wrong_end_of_the_axis_when_reverse_x_axis_reverse_y_axis_is_set", "label": "MOT-07 - Held jog and step jog drive the head to the wrong end of the axis when reverse_x_axis / reverse_y_axis is set", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L585"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_08_a_failed_position_read_makes_the_jog_origin_0_0_turning_a_10_mm_jog_into_a_full_bed_traverse_to_the_machine_corner", "label": "MOT-08 - A failed position read makes the jog origin (0, 0), turning a 10 mm jog into a full-bed traverse to the machine corner", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L706"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_09_stop_during_a_cut_scale_calls_cancel_frame_which_cannot_stop_a_job_the_laser_keeps_cutting", "label": "MOT-09 - Stop during a Cut Scale calls cancel_frame(), which cannot stop a job \u2014 the laser keeps cutting", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L788"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_10_wait_for_job_completion_can_never_exit_against_an_unresponsive_controller_and_it_holds_suppress_polling_so_the_connection_loop_s_watchdog_stays_disarmed", "label": "MOT-10 - _wait_for_job_completion can never exit against an unresponsive controller, and it holds _suppress_polling so the connection loop's watchdog stays disarmed", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L879"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_11_home_is_not_tracked_as_busy_and_its_completion_wait_is_satisfied_by_any_position_reply_including_the_background_poller_s", "label": "MOT-11 - home() is not tracked as busy and its completion wait is satisfied by any position reply, including the background poller's", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L964"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_12_jog_key_down_leaks_jog_busy_true_when_jog_to_limit_finds_an_emptied_key_set_bricking_every_further_jog_until_the_panel_is_unmapped", "label": "MOT-12 - jog_key_down leaks _jog_busy=True when _jog_to_limit finds an emptied key set, bricking every further jog until the panel is unmapped", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1061"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_13_z_jog_deltas_are_silently_discarded_by_both_ruida_jog_paths_while_the_z_buttons_stay_enabled_and_a_z_hold_leaks_jog_busy", "label": "MOT-13 - Z jog deltas are silently discarded by both Ruida jog paths while the Z buttons stay enabled, and a Z hold leaks _jog_busy", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1168"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_14_wait_for_jog_settled_always_computes_a_zero_travel_distance_so_a_step_jog_gives_up_after_1_s_and_the_next_step_is_measured_from_a_mid_move_position", "label": "MOT-14 - _wait_for_jog_settled always computes a zero travel distance, so a step jog gives up after 1 s and the next step is measured from a mid-move position", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1258"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_15_eventcontrollermotion_leave_never_fires_while_the_button_is_held_so_dragging_off_does_not_stop_the_jog", "label": "MOT-15 - EventControllerMotion 'leave' never fires while the button is held, so dragging off does not stop the jog", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1328"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_16_interactive_commands_are_dispatched_as_unkeyed_taskmanager_coroutines_which_gives_them_no_ordering_at_all", "label": "MOT-16 - Interactive commands are dispatched as unkeyed TaskManager coroutines, which gives them no ordering at all", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1421"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_17_a_single_0xcc_from_any_interactive_command_pops_the_head_of_pending_job_acks_and_falsely_acknowledges_an_outstanding_job_chunk", "label": "MOT-17 - A single 0xCC from any interactive command pops the head of _pending_job_acks and falsely acknowledges an outstanding job chunk", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1515"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_18_da_replies_are_attributed_by_address_alone_so_the_connection_loop_s_un_futured_position_poll_answers_an_interactive_read_that_had_not_been_sent_yet", "label": "MOT-18 - DA replies are attributed by address alone, so the connection loop's un-futured position poll answers an interactive read that had not been sent yet", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1613"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_19_response_received_is_set_by_every_decoded_packet_so_a_bare_transport_ack_satisfies_the_connection_loop_s_liveness_wait_and_masks_a_controller_that_has_stopped_answering_position_reads", "label": "MOT-19 - _response_received is set by every decoded packet, so a bare transport ACK satisfies the connection loop's liveness wait and masks a controller that has stopped answering position reads", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1694"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_20_pending_mem_reads_holds_one_future_per_address_a_second_overlapping_read_of_the_same_address_orphans_the_first_and_the_orphan_s_timeout_evicts_a_stranger_s_future", "label": "MOT-20 - _pending_mem_reads holds one future per address: a second overlapping read of the same address orphans the first, and the orphan's timeout evicts a stranger's future", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1778"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_resolve_waiters_self_pending_mem_reads_get_mem_address_while", "label": "resolve: waiters = self._pending_mem_reads.get(mem_address) # while", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1854"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_timeout_waiters_self_pending_mem_reads_get_mem_address_if", "label": "timeout: waiters = self._pending_mem_reads.get(mem_address, []) # if", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1856"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_21_hold_jog_speed_defaults_to_12000_mm_min_200_mm_s_and_is_never_synced_from_the_ui_so_a_press_and_hold_runs_12x_faster_than_the_jog_speed_row_shows", "label": "MOT-21 - Hold-jog speed defaults to 12000 mm/min (200 mm/s) and is never synced from the UI, so a press-and-hold runs 12x faster than the Jog Speed row shows", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1882"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_22_the_connection_loop_never_sends_a_keepalive_after_the_first_and_its_1_0_s_sleep_makes_position_poll_interval_0_5_unreachable", "label": "MOT-22 - The connection loop never sends a keepalive after the first, and its 1.0 s sleep makes POSITION_POLL_INTERVAL=0.5 unreachable", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L1969"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_23_home_zeroes_the_machine_but_never_invalidates_last_known_pos_only_x_is_corrected_by_accident", "label": "MOT-23 - home() zeroes the machine but never invalidates _last_known_pos; only X is corrected, by accident", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2038"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_24_go_scale_outlines_the_box_at_the_current_head_position_but_the_job_and_cut_scale_cut_it_at_the_ref0_anchor", "label": "MOT-24 - Go Scale outlines the box at the current head position, but the job (and Cut Scale) cut it at the REF0 anchor", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2118"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_25_suppress_polling_is_one_boolean_with_two_owners_trace_frame_s_exit_re_enables_position_polling_in_the_middle_of_a_job_upload", "label": "MOT-25 - _suppress_polling is one boolean with two owners: trace_frame's exit re-enables position polling in the middle of a job upload", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2220"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_26_go_scale_hard_codes_100_mm_s_and_is_the_only_travel_path_that_ignores_the_profile_s_max_travel_speed", "label": "MOT-26 - Go Scale hard-codes 100 mm/s and is the only travel path that ignores the profile's max travel speed", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2286"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_27_jog_key_up_sets_jog_busy_true_outside_any_try_finally_an_error_from_jog_to_limit_leaks_the_flag_and_blocks_every_step_jog", "label": "MOT-27 - jog_key_up sets _jog_busy = True outside any try/finally; an error from _jog_to_limit leaks the flag and blocks every step jog", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2365"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_28_stop_jog_motion_leaves_the_commanded_bed_limit_target_cached_when_the_resync_read_fails_so_the_next_step_jog_runs_to_the_far_end_of_the_bed", "label": "MOT-28 - _stop_jog_motion leaves the commanded bed-limit target cached when the resync read fails, so the next step jog runs to the far end of the bed", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2432"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_29_stop_jog_motion_clears_jog_busy_regardless_of_who_owns_it_dropping_go_scale_s_ignore_interlock", "label": "MOT-29 - _stop_jog_motion clears _jog_busy regardless of who owns it, dropping Go Scale's ignore interlock", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2507"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_30_go_scale_corners_are_silently_clamped_to_the_bed_so_the_traced_rectangle_is_not_the_job_s_size", "label": "MOT-30 - Go Scale corners are silently clamped to the bed, so the traced rectangle is not the job's size", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2578"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_31_on_position_updated_invents_0_for_the_axis_it_has_not_seen_yet_so_a_jog_landing_between_the_x_and_y_position_responses_drives_y_to_the_bed_edge", "label": "MOT-31 - _on_position_updated invents 0 for the axis it has not seen yet, so a jog landing between the X and Y position responses drives Y to the bed edge", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2644"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_32_jog_speed_round_trips_base_display_int_mm_s_base_quantising_to_60_mm_min_steps_and_forcing_a_60_mm_min_floor_at_the_bottom_of_the_row_s_range", "label": "MOT-32 - Jog speed round-trips base -> display -> int(mm/s) -> base, quantising to 60 mm/min steps and forcing a 60 mm/min floor at the bottom of the row's range", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2712"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_33_jogwidget_jog_speed_defaults_to_100_mm_s_six_times_the_jog_speed_row_s_own_default_so_a_click_jog_runs_at_6000_mm_min_while_the_panel_reads_1000_mm_min", "label": "MOT-33 - JogWidget.jog_speed defaults to 100 mm/s, six times the Jog Speed row's own default, so a click-jog runs at 6000 mm/min while the panel reads 1000 mm/min", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2794"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_34_arrow_key_jog_has_no_key_release_handler_and_no_repeat_guard_each_repeat_queues_an_unkeyed_task", "label": "MOT-34 - Arrow-key jog has no key-release handler and no repeat guard; each repeat queues an unkeyed task", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2873"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_35_update_button_sensitivity_flips_every_jog_button_insensitive_which_cancels_an_in_flight_press", "label": "MOT-35 - _update_button_sensitivity flips every jog button insensitive, which cancels an in-flight press", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L2953"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_36_one_hold_timer_for_every_arrow_a_second_press_kills_the_first_s_hold_and_any_release_kills_whichever_hold_is_armed", "label": "MOT-36 - One hold timer for every arrow: a second press kills the first's hold, and any release kills whichever hold is armed", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L3027"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_37_held_keys_are_released_by_axis_sign_identity_not_by_the_button_that_pressed_them", "label": "MOT-37 - Held keys are released by (axis,sign) identity, not by the button that pressed them", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L3106"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_38_d9_10_targets_are_documented_as_anchor_relative_but_fed_absolute_machine_coordinates_read_back_from_0x0421_0x0431", "label": "MOT-38 - D9 10 targets are documented as anchor-relative but fed absolute machine coordinates read back from 0x0421/0x0431", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L3186"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_39_the_repo_s_only_modelled_motion_stop_primitive_and_the_whole_jog_udp_channel_are_dead_code", "label": "MOT-39 - The repo's only modelled motion-stop primitive, and the whole jog UDP channel, are dead code", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "MOTION_AUDIT.md", "source_location": "L3288"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_motion_audit_mot_40_d9_00_d9_01_have_three